               "format": "markdown",
               "PostMention": ""
            },
            {
               "text": "<p><div class=\"htSlides\"><div class=\"htSlide\"><div class=\"htSlideCounter\">1 / 2</div><img class=\"imgGameSize\" id=\"imgUSGS0\" onclick=\"htImageZoom('imgUSGS0', '0%')\"><div class=\"htSlideCaption\">Water Cycle. Public domain image from the U.S. Geological Survey (<htcite0>).</div><div class=\"htSlideRefs\"><b>Related content:</b><ul><li>Shared Origin - After observing different ways of grouping and counting quantities, we moved on to studying the sharing of those quantities. (<htcite1>)</li><li>Cooking - The preparation of food is often remembered for adding quantities, but there is also another side to it. (<htcite2>)</li><li>Texts with Sciences (Part II) - After exploring some figures of speech present in ancient texts, a question arises: what was the context of the Flood? (<htcite3>)</li></ul></div></div><div class=\"htSlide\"><div class=\"htSlideCounter\">2 / 2</div><img class=\"imgGameSize\" id=\"imgUSG\" onclick=\"htImageZoom('imgUSG', '0%')\"><div class=\"htSlideCaption\">Water Cycle (in Spanish). Public domain image from the U.S. Geological Survey (<htcite4>).</div><div class=\"htSlideRefs\"><b>Related content:</b><ul><li>Tang Dynasty (唐代) - Nearly 300 years of significant advances, innovations, and possible long-distance trade relations. (<htcite5>)</li></ul></div></div><i class=\"fa-solid fa-chevron-left htSlidePrev\" onclick=\"htPlusDivs(-1);\"></i><i class=\"fa-solid fa-chevron-right htSlideNext\" onclick=\"htPlusDivs(1);\"></i></div></p>",
